## Non-Claude Tools (Cursor, Copilot, etc.) {#non-claude-tools}

**CRITICAL**: Claude Code has automatic hooks. Other tools DO NOT.

### What's Different

| Feature | Claude Code | Cursor/Copilot |
|---------|-------------|----------------|
| Commands | Slash syntax works | Manual workflow |
| Hooks | Auto-run on events | None |
| Task sync | Automatic | Manual |
| GitHub sync | Automatic | Manual |

### Manual Command Execution

In non-Claude tools, commands are markdown workflows. Execute them manually:

```bash
# Step 1: Find the command file
cat plugins/specweave/commands/specweave-increment.md

# Step 2: Read the workflow instructions
# Step 3: Execute each step manually
# Step 4: Update tasks.md when done
```

### After EVERY Task Completion (MANDATORY)

```bash
# 1. Update tasks.md source of truth
/specweave:sync-tasks

# 2. Sync to living docs
/specweave:sync-docs update

# 3. Sync to external tracker (if enabled)
/specweave-github:sync <increment-id>
```

Without these manual syncs, your progress won't be tracked!

